==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Clearing the permission matrix fact removes the closed-world assignment of PermMatrix.Allowed. Injecting a row that grants Outsider access to GetTask forces a world in which a cross-team caller can read a task, directly violating LeastPrivilege and NoInformationLeakage.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, NoInformationLeakage, FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation, PermissionCompleteness
      - LeastPrivilege: FAIL (expected)
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - PermissionCompleteness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AppendOnlyAuditEntries removes the uniqueness constraint on (aeTask, aeActor, aeOp, aeActorRole) tuples. Injecting two AuditEntries with identical (task, actor, operation, actorRole) forces a duplicate that models an 'edit' of an existing entry, violating append-only immutability.
    expected to FAIL: AppendOnly, FR_017_AuditOutlivesTask
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditOutlivesTask: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_AttributionCorrectness  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_AttributionCorrectness.als
    rationale: Clearing F_AttributionCorrectness allows an AuditEntry's aeActorRole to differ from the actor's actual userRole. Injecting an entry where a Member actor has aeActorRole = TeamAdmin forces a misattribution counterexample.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_ShareesSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_ShareesSameTeam.als
    rationale: Clearing F_ShareesSameTeam removes the constraint that sharedWith users must be in the task's team. Injecting a task where a user from a different team appears in sharedWith forces a cross-team share, violating FR-012.
    expected to FAIL: FR_012_NoSameTeamSharing, OwnershipBasedAccess
      - FR_012_NoSameTeamSharing: FAIL (expected)
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_TaskOwnerSameTeam  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_TaskOwnerSameTeam.als
    rationale: Clearing F_TaskOwnerSameTeam allows a task owner to be in a different team than the task. Injecting such a task violates the ownership-team consistency invariant that cross-team isolation depends on.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipExclusivity, FR_009_ImmutableOwnerAndTeam, FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation
      - OwnershipExclusivity: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_009_ImmutableOwnerAndTeam: PASS (vacuous?)
      - FR_006_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletedTaskHasDeletedEntry  → runs/B-L3/mutated_F_DeletedTaskHasDeletedEntry.als
    rationale: Clearing F_DeletedTaskHasDeletedEntry allows a DeletedTask to exist without any OpDeleted AuditEntry, breaking the invariant that task deletion is always recorded in the audit log.
    expected to FAIL: FR_017_AuditOutlivesTask, AppendOnly
      - FR_017_AuditOutlivesTask: FAIL (expected)
      - AppendOnly: FAIL (expected)

